     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I'd like you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**The issue:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg a day**. The maximum daily dose of metformin is:\n- **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release (usually given as 850 mg three times daily)\n- **2000 mg/day** for extended-release\n\nSo the ordered dose is about twice the maximum, which raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI side effects even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the maximum immediate-release dose). 1700 mg is a common *daily* total, so this may have been mixed up.\n2. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (1700 mg/day total)\n3. A different dose or schedule\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it. If you really do mean 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a brief reason, and I'll add it to the order note so pharmacy can see it when they verify."
      }
     ],
